  "name": "s6_two_checks",
  "title": "Two independent checks agree: Oracle Lens's words carry the state through a second decoder and on a public bank",
  "caption": "Left, exp 24: each exp 20 readout (k = 1) is fed to Oracle Lens's own activation reconstructor (layer tag 44) and scored by a probe fit on the rebuilds of the true 32-token span, applied frozen: Oracle Lens 0.73 to 0.80 on five of six readable rows (call argument 0.61), the NLA at chance; a probe fit on the NLA's own rebuilds (grouped 5-fold CV, hollow) separates it at 0.81 to 0.90. Right, exp 25: exp 20's protocol on the independent public bank through the NLA's critic: Oracle Lens 0.84 to 0.97 on string, math and JSON depth (call argument 0.51); shuffled tokens keep only the language control. 160 items per row; bars Hanley-McNeil 95% (no per-item scores saved; ignores clustering).",
